Linking each name to its WoRMS record shows how far the names in the inventory differ from
current taxonomy. WoRMS gives a different accepted name for {{ q03.n }} of the names used in the
article (Table 4):

- **{{ q03.valid | Words }} names the article uses as valid.** For {{ q03.valid_changed | words }} of them the accepted
  name differs. *Parazoanthus catenularis* is now *Bergia catenularis*, its original combination,
  restored when {{ citet("montenegro2015") }} resurrected *Bergia*; *Corynactis caribbeorum* is
  again *Pseudocorynactis caribbeorum*, restored by {{ citet("ocana2017") }} after
  {{ citet("fautin2011") }} had sunk the genus. *Exaiptasia pallida* is a junior subjective synonym of
  *E. diaphana*: the Commission declined to give *pallida* precedence {{ cite("iczn2017") }} and
  declined to reverse that ruling {{ cite("iczn2019", "iczn2023") }}. Those rulings fix the name only
  if the two are one species; the article's *E. pallida* is a worldwide concept, and the WoRMS
  record, last modified before the second ruling, still reads "pallida valid until ICZN rules
  Case 3790".
- **{{ q03.invalid | Words }} names the article itself marks with †**, which its legend defines as "species
  currently considered as invalid". One, *Anthopleura cascaia*, is a nomen nudum: an unavailable
  name, which cannot be a synonym. WoRMS links it to *A. correae*, described by
  {{ citet("duranfuentes2025") }}, whose authors include the source article's first author; the
  present author is not among them. The link is a judgement about the intended species, not a
  synonymy.
- **{{ q03.label | Words }} previous identifications of museum specimens.** Across all
  {{ e.id_changes.values() | sum }} specimens whose identification Table 3 changed, the coded reasons are
  {% for k, v in e.id_changes.items() | sort %}{{ v }} {{ k }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}: most are name updates,
  not re-identifications.
- **{{ q03.spelling | Words }} orthographic variants**: *Bunodosoma cavernata*, which WoRMS holds as an
  unaccepted record of *B. cavernatum*, and three misspellings that matched the accepted record
  directly.

Whether the article lagged behind published taxonomy depends on the act that fixes today's
name, not on the sources WoRMS cites, some of which are not acts. Of the {{ q03.n }} changes,
{{ q03.before | words }} rest on an act published before the article was submitted ({{ f.submitted_date }}), the
